<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_8_8" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_8_8" name="8.8 Manage distribution integrity programme" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>Five of the seven processes are drawn. 8.8.1 the written programme and 8.8.3 the risk ranking are SPEC.

THIS IS THE ONLY COMPLETE MANAGEMENT CYCLE IN THE REFERENCE THAT A REGULATION WRITES OUT IN FULL. 49 CFR 192.1007 names seven elements in order - (a) know the infrastructure, (b) identify threats, (c) evaluate and rank risk, (d) identify and implement measures, (e) measure performance, (f) periodically evaluate and improve, (g) report results - and the flow follows them rather than a cycle of the author's. Where the rest of the library derives a sequence from consensus or judgment, this one is the rule.

8.8.3 IS SPEC AND THAT IS THE FINDING. 192.1007(c) requires the evaluation and prescribes NO method. Drawing it as a decision table would mean inventing the ranking rule and then citing the CFR for it, which the CFR does not support. The gap is recorded rather than filled.

TWO BOUNDARIES ARE DRAWN AS HANDOVERS. 12.6.2 assesses an ASSET on the operator's own method and is not regulatory; this ranks THREATS to the system under a federal rule, and both are kept because not all asset risk assessment is regulatory. And 8.8.7 produces and validates the four reportable measures while 15.3.1 files the report - producing a number and submitting it have different owners and different evidence. Both ruled by Tim, 2026-08-30.

Gas distribution only. 16 U.S.C. 824o excludes local distribution of electric energy from the bulk-power system, and no electric distribution integrity management regime exists at federal level at all.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_8_8_lanes">
      <lane id="l_88_int" name="Integrity management">
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_know</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_thr</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_attr</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_rank</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_ast</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_sel</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_how</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_re</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_88_del" name="Delivery and reporting">
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_work</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_cap</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_meas</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_four</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_88_file</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_88_start" name="The programme cycle opens"><timerEventDefinition id="n_88_start_td"/></startEvent>
    <receiveTask id="n_88_know" name="Take the written programme and system knowledge"><documentation>8.8.1, SPEC. 192.1007(a). Recorded GAPS in knowledge are an input, not an embarrassment: an unknown material or vintage is itself a threat characteristic.</documentation></receiveTask>
    <userTask id="n_88_thr" name="Identify existing and potential threats"><documentation>8.8.2. 192.1007(b). Inputs include 8.2.5 internal corrosion, 8.3.4 leak backlog, 8.4.5 damage statistics and 8.7.1 cross bore risk - named evidence, not incidental history.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_88_attr" name="Attribute each threat to what it reaches"><documentation>8.8.2. A threat identified generically for the whole system tells the ranking nothing.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_88_rank" name="Evaluate and rank the risk"><documentation>8.8.3, SPEC. 192.1007(c) requires the evaluation and prescribes no method. The method and its uncertainty are recorded WITH the rank or it cannot be re-evaluated at 8.8.6.</documentation></sendTask>
    <sendTask id="n_88_ast" name="Asset-level risk, where it is procedure rather than rule"><documentation>12.6.2. Kept separate because not all asset risk assessment is regulatory.</documentation></sendTask>
    <userTask id="n_88_sel" name="Select the risk-reduction measures"><documentation>8.8.4. 192.1007(d) requires identification AND implementation; identifying alone does not satisfy the element.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_88_how" name="How the measure is delivered"/>
    <sendTask id="n_88_work" name="Release as maintenance or inspection work"><documentation>8.8.4. Tracked against the THREAT it was selected for, not against the work order.</documentation></sendTask>
    <sendTask id="n_88_cap" name="Compete it in the capital programme at 17.4"><documentation>8.8.4. The integrity rank is an input to that competition, not an authorisation to spend.</documentation></sendTask>
    <businessRuleTask id="n_88_meas" name="Measure performance against the baseline"><documentation>8.8.5. 192.1007(e). Against the BASELINE the programme set, not against last period.</documentation></businessRuleTask>
    <userTask id="n_88_four" name="Produce and validate the four reportable measures"><documentation>8.8.7. 192.1007(e) and (g), reported under 191.11. Reconciliation precedes the number.</documentation></userTask>
    <sendTask id="n_88_file" name="Hand the validated measures to 15.3.1 to file"><documentation>8.8.7. 15.3.1 submits. This process does not file anything.</documentation></sendTask>
    <userTask id="n_88_re" name="Re-evaluate the programme and improve it"><documentation>8.8.6. 192.1007(f). 192.1013 requires a deviation to be reported - a quiet change is how a deviation becomes invisible.</documentation></userTask>
    <endEvent id="n_88_end" name="Programme cycle closed and reissued"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_start_n_88_know" sourceRef="n_88_start" targetRef="n_88_know" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_know_n_88_thr" sourceRef="n_88_know" targetRef="n_88_thr" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_thr_n_88_attr" sourceRef="n_88_thr" targetRef="n_88_attr" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_attr_n_88_rank" sourceRef="n_88_attr" targetRef="n_88_rank" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_attr_n_88_ast" sourceRef="n_88_attr" targetRef="n_88_ast" name="asset-level, non-regulatory"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_rank_n_88_sel" sourceRef="n_88_rank" targetRef="n_88_sel" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_sel_n_88_how" sourceRef="n_88_sel" targetRef="n_88_how" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_how_n_88_work" sourceRef="n_88_how" targetRef="n_88_work" name="work"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_how_n_88_cap" sourceRef="n_88_how" targetRef="n_88_cap" name="replacement programme"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_how_n_88_meas" sourceRef="n_88_how" targetRef="n_88_meas" name="procedure or training change"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_work_n_88_meas" sourceRef="n_88_work" targetRef="n_88_meas" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_cap_n_88_meas" sourceRef="n_88_cap" targetRef="n_88_meas" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_meas_n_88_four" sourceRef="n_88_meas" targetRef="n_88_four" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_four_n_88_file" sourceRef="n_88_four" targetRef="n_88_file" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_file_n_88_re" sourceRef="n_88_file" targetRef="n_88_re" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_88_re_n_88_end" sourceRef="n_88_re" targetRef="n_88_end" name=""/>
  </process>
